00:56:49,090 --> 00:56:55,090
The Electric State is a 2025 American science fiction action-adventure
film produced and directed by Anthony and Joe Russo.

11
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:36,000
Its screenplay by Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely is loosely
based on the 2018 illustrated novel by Simon Stålenhag.

12
01:08:10,909 --> 01:08:16,909
The film stars Millie Bobby Brown, Chris Pratt, Ke Huy Quan (in a dual role), Jason Alexander, Woody
Harrelson, Anthony Mackie, Brian Cox, Jenny Slate, Giancarlo Esposito and Stanley Tucci.

13
01:13:51,818 --> 01:13:57,818
Plans for a film adaptation were announced in 2017, with Andy Muschietti.

14
01:19:32,727 --> 01:19:38,727
The Russo brothers signed on to direct in December 2020.

15
01:25:13,636 --> 01:25:19,636
Universal Pictures acquired the distribution rights before
Netflix took over the rights in June 2022.

16
01:30:54,545 --> 01:31:00,545
Much of the cast was revealed between June 2022 and November 2024, with
filming taking place in Atlanta, Georgia in fall 2022.

17
01:36:35,454 --> 01:36:41,454
With a reported budget of $320 million, it is one of
the most expensive films ever made.

18
01:42:16,363 --> 01:42:22,363
The Electric State premiered at Grauman's Egyptian Theatre in Los Angeles on
February 24, 2025, and was released on Netflix on March 14.

19
01:47:57,272 --> 01:48:03,272
It received negative reviews from critics.

20
01:53:38,181 --> 01:53:44,181
The film explores themes of man vs machine, artificial intelligence
(a.i.), based on novel or book, technology, dystopia.

21
01:59:19,090 --> 01:59:25,090
The tone is thought_provoking.
